---
import HarnessStage from './HarnessStage.astro';
import { phaseFor, type Scene } from '../scripts/harness-storyboard';
import '../styles/harness-walkthrough.css';

interface Chapter {
  id: string;
  scene: Scene;
  label: string;
  title: string;
  body: string[];
  aliases?: string[];
  link?: { href: string; text: string };
}

const chapters: Chapter[] = [
  {
    id: 'compose-a-domain-specific-harness',
    scene: 'basics', label: 'Agent skills',
    title: 'Start with an agent skill.',
    aliases: ['the-first-run'],
    body: [
      'Teams today can give an agent a skill: reusable instructions for a task, sometimes bundled with scripts or reference files.',
      'A skill helps the agent do its part. A larger process still needs someone to decide how skills work together, which tools they can call, and when a person needs to review the result.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'where-the-work-breaks',
    scene: 'tangled', label: 'Custom wiring',
    title: 'Then wire the pieces together.',
    body: [
      'When teams stitch skills and tools together with custom scripts, handoffs depend on local conventions. One skill’s result may need reshaping before the next can use it.',
      'Moving the workflow to a new team can mean rebuilding those handoffs and access rules. An expert’s correction can be lost before the next run.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'inside-a-playbook',
    scene: 'contract', label: 'The playbook contract',
    title: 'The spec starts with standard playbooks.',
    aliases: ['composed-architecture', 'where-the-spec-starts'],
    body: [
      'The Domain-Specific Agent Harness Spec proposes a shared way to define and compose workflows. Gabriel calls the reusable unit a playbook. It declares its inputs, steps, outputs, connector operations, and approval rules.',
      'A playbook can use skills for instructions and domain knowledge. Its steps declare the capabilities they need. The workspace binds those capabilities when the playbook runs, so the team can reuse the same definition.',
    ],
    link: { href: './concepts/teams-and-goals/', text: 'The playbook contract' },
  },
  {
    id: 'teams-inside-a-persona',
    scene: 'persona', label: 'Standard composition',
    title: 'Compose teams into a persona.',
    aliases: ['map-the-ontology'],
    body: [
      'A persona brings together teams. Each team contains its goals and the playbooks they use. The domain ontology maps the organization’s apps and data into shared concepts, so those teams agree on what the work means.',
      'A persona can work with text, speech, images, video, and audio. A spoken request can use speech-to-speech directly or use speech-to-text, a text model, and text-to-speech.',
    ],
    link: { href: './concepts/personas-and-workspaces/', text: 'Personas and workspaces' },
  },
  {
    id: 'how-it-works',
    scene: 'goals', label: 'Goals invoke playbooks',
    title: 'The goal chooses the work.',
    aliases: ['how-does-a-persona-work', 'goal-to-playbook', 'bind-models-and-modalities'],
    body: [
      'Create a goal inside a team. The goal selects and invokes the playbooks that belong to that team, in the order the outcome and their dependencies require.',
      'Agents run the selected playbooks and skills inside the harness. The workspace binds models to the capabilities each step needs through a compatible provider or gateway. Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, Grok, and Kimi K2 are examples.',
    ],
    link: { href: './concepts/teams-and-goals/#from-an-outcome-to-a-plan', text: 'From a goal to a plan' },
  },
  {
    id: 'create-a-missing-playbook',
    scene: 'missing', label: 'Create a missing playbook',
    title: 'Missing a playbook? Create it.',
    body: [
      'When a goal reveals a missing capability, the team can draft a playbook for it. The new definition declares its inputs, steps, outputs, and connector requirements.',
      'Review and register it before adding it to a plan. Later goals can reuse the reviewed definition.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'connect-the-work',
    scene: 'connectors', label: 'Connectors and data',
    title: 'Connect playbooks to real data.',
    aliases: ['from-git-to-a-running-workspace'],
    body: [
      'During execution, playbooks use connectors to retrieve data, update records, and share results with external services.',
      'The harness resolves each required operation to an authorized connection. The same domain mappings make the data understandable across the team.',
    ],
    link: { href: './apps/#2-connector-requirements-', text: 'Connector requirements' },
  },
  {
    id: 'credentials-in-the-vault',
    scene: 'vault', label: 'Vault and credentials',
    title: 'The vault holds the credentials.',
    body: [
      'A connector describes the operations available. Its connection uses the credentials stored in the vault to access the selected account.',
      'Reusing a playbook does not copy someone else’s access. Each workspace binds the required connectors to its own authorized accounts.',
    ],
    link: { href: './concepts/connectors-and-approvals/#credentials-stay-in-the-vault', text: 'Connections and the vault' },
  },
  {
    id: 'use-the-mapped-data',
    scene: 'apps', label: 'Custom apps',
    title: 'Build apps on the same connections.',
    body: [
      'Agents can create custom apps that read connector data and display it as graphs, tables, or working interfaces. Apps can also consume the outputs that playbooks produce.',
      'Agents use authorized operations to write changes back to the source services or the custom app’s data. The app gives people a place to see and work with the result, including through an externally hosted interface.',
    ],
    link: { href: './apps/#6-custom-app-packages-', text: 'Custom apps and installations' },
  },
  {
    id: 'learn-from-approvals',
    scene: 'review', label: 'Governed execution',
    title: 'Rehearse the change. Then approve it.',
    body: [
      'When the team’s goal calls for a change to app data, the playbook drafts the action. A domain specialist can clarify the scope or correct the plan. The harness rehearses the proposed change in a sandbox with live effects disabled.',
      'The specialist reviews the rehearsal and approves the exact action. The harness rechecks the approval before sending the action through the same connector shown above. The live receipt and the specialist’s feedback inform the next reviewed playbook revision.',
    ],
    link: { href: './concepts/governed-execution/', text: 'Human review and sandbox rehearsal' },
  },
  {
    id: 'reuse-a-playbook',
    scene: 'reuse', label: 'Reuse across personas',
    title: 'Scale by reusing the work.',
    body: [
      'A playbook from the registry can serve several teams, including teams in different personas. Each goal invokes the work it needs with its own inputs and domain mappings.',
      'Each workspace keeps its own connector accounts, vault, data, and approvals. A reviewed package revision can be adopted without rebuilding the entire composition.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'the-complete-harness',
    scene: 'complete', label: 'The complete harness',
    title: 'This is a domain-specific harness.',
    body: [
      'A persona groups playbooks into teams around a domain model. Goals inside each team invoke the playbooks they need. A missing capability can guide a new playbook draft. Agents execute that work inside the harness, using the skills and model capabilities each step needs.',
      'Connectors move the data. The vault supplies account credentials. Custom apps make the data and results usable. Domain specialists guide decisions, review rehearsals, and approve protected effects. Run evidence helps them improve the harness.',
    ],
    link: { href: './specification/', text: 'Explore the specification' },
  },
  {
    id: 'playbook-marketplace',
    scene: 'marketplace', label: 'Marketplace',
    title: 'Mix and match playbooks to build personas.',
    aliases: ['persona-marketplace', 'package-a-playbook'],
    body: [
      'The proposed marketplace lets teams discover standard playbook packages and combine them into personas. Pair Research with Verify to build a research analyst, or pair Research with Draft to build a briefing writer.',
      'Authors can publish individual playbooks or list a complete persona when they want to share the whole setup. Team definitions pin the playbook revisions they use.',
    ],
    link: { href: './concepts/teams-and-goals/#reuse-a-playbook', text: 'Packages and reuse' },
  },
];
---

<div class="hs-story not-content" data-harness-story>
  <div class="hs-chapters">
    {chapters.map((chapter) => (
      <article class="hs-chapter" id={chapter.id} data-hs-chapter={chapter.scene} data-hs-spec-start={chapter.scene === 'contract' ? '' : undefined}>
        {chapter.aliases?.map(id => <span id={id} class="hs-anchor"></span>)}
        <div class="hs-copy">
          <p class="hs-kicker"><span>{phaseFor(chapter.scene)}</span> · {chapter.label}</p>
          <h3>{chapter.title}</h3>
          {chapter.body.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
          {chapter.link && <a href={chapter.link.href}>{chapter.link.text} →</a>}
        </div>
        <HarnessStage scene={chapter.scene} />
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>

  <aside class="hs-sticky" aria-label="Walkthrough diagrams" data-hs-sticky hidden>
    <HarnessStage />
    <nav class="hs-progress" aria-label="Walkthrough chapters">
      {chapters.map(chapter => (
        <a href={'#' + chapter.id} aria-label={phaseFor(chapter.scene) + ' · ' + chapter.label} title={chapter.label} data-hs-jump></a>
      ))}
    </nav>
  </aside>
</div>

<script>
  import { mountHarnessScene } from '../scripts/harness-motion';
  import type { Scene } from '../scripts/harness-storyboard';

  for (const story of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-harness-story]')) {
    const chapters = [...story.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-hs-chapter]')];
    const sticky = story.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-hs-sticky]');
    const stage = story.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-hs-stage]');
    const links = [...story.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('[data-hs-jump]')];
    if (!sticky || !stage || !chapters.length) continue;

    const wide = matchMedia('(min-width: 54rem) and (min-height: 36rem)');
    const reducedMotion = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
    const scenes = chapters.map(chapter => chapter.dataset.hsChapter as Scene);
    let visual: ReturnType<typeof mountHarnessScene>;
    let eyeLine = 0;
    let active = -1;
    let frame = 0;

    const setActive = (index: number) => {
      if (active === index) return;
      links[active]?.removeAttribute('aria-current');
      chapters[active]?.removeAttribute('data-hs-active');
      active = index;
      links[index]?.setAttribute('aria-current', 'step');
      chapters[index]?.setAttribute('data-hs-active', '');
    };

    const render = (index: number, progress = 0) => {
      const current = progress >= 0.5 ? index + 1 : index;
      if (reducedMotion.matches || progress === 0 || progress === 1) {
        visual?.render(scenes[current], scenes[current], 0);
      } else {
        visual?.render(scenes[index], scenes[index + 1], progress);
      }

      setActive(current);
    };

    const center = (chapter: HTMLElement) => {
      const { top, height } = chapter.getBoundingClientRect();
      return top + height / 2;
    };

    const measure = () => {
      let from = center(chapters[0]);
      if (eyeLine <= from) {
        render(0);
        return;
      }

      for (let i = 1; i < chapters.length; i++) {
        const to = center(chapters[i]);
        if (eyeLine <= to) {
          const fraction = (eyeLine - from) / (to - from);
          const progress = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (fraction - 0.26) / 0.48));
          render(i - 1, progress);
          return;
        }
        from = to;
      }

      render(chapters.length - 1);
    };

    const schedule = () => {
      if (!wide.matches || frame) return;
      frame = requestAnimationFrame(() => {
        frame = 0;
        if (wide.matches) measure();
      });
    };

    const resize = () => {
      eyeLine = Math.min(innerHeight * 0.48, 23 * parseFloat(getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).fontSize));
      visual?.resize();
      schedule();
    };

    const updateLayout = () => {
      if (wide.matches && !visual) visual = mountHarnessScene(stage);
      story.toggleAttribute('data-hs-ready', wide.matches && Boolean(visual));
      sticky.hidden = !wide.matches || !visual;
      if (!sticky.hidden) {
        resize();
        measure();
      }
    };

    new ResizeObserver(resize).observe(story);

    updateLayout();
    wide.addEventListener('change', updateLayout);
    reducedMotion.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    addEventListener('scroll', schedule, { passive: true });
    addEventListener('resize', resize);
    addEventListener('pageshow', schedule);
  }
</script>
